// A `for` loop carrying a literal-union value (owner ruling 2026-09-29): the loop can run out,
// so the value is `AB | null`, whose binding is spelled by its members and holds the atom niche.
// The proof reads the member the break chose.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type AB = "a" | "b"
function pickB(): AB { "b" }
// @@VALUE@@
for i in 0 until 3 { if i == 1 { break pickB() } }
// @@TYPE@@
AB | null
// @@PROOF@@
if v == "b" { print("b") } else { print("other") }
// @@WANT@@
b
